<title>USA: Cooper Tire &amp; Rubber sells $200 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Cooper Tire &amp; Rubber sells $200 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from Cooper Tire and Rubber Co was priced on Thursday, according to sole manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>Cooper Tire and Rubber makes private-label tires for auto and truck replacement markets.</p>
<p>BORROWER COOPER TIRE AND RUBBER CO</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.625 PCT  MATURITY 3/15/2027</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 98.875  FIRST PAY DATE 9/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD 7.722 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 70 BPS     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
